; DSOUND.dll as the DirectX 5 SDK's dsound.lib knew it, which the game was
; linked with. DirectX 5 added DirectSoundCapture, whose three exports sort
; before DirectSoundCreate, so its hint (the index of the name in the DLL's
; sorted export table) is 3, as the original's import table has it; the
; toolchain's DSOUND.LIB is DirectX 3's, with 0. LIB numbers the hints in the
; order of the sorted names. Each name is spelled as its __stdcall symbol is;
; tools/place.py builds the import library from this file and the import
; tables from that.
LIBRARY DSOUND
EXPORTS
    DirectSoundCaptureCreate@12
    DirectSoundCaptureEnumerateA@8
    DirectSoundCaptureEnumerateW@8
    DirectSoundCreate@12
    DirectSoundEnumerateA@8
    DirectSoundEnumerateW@8
    DllCanUnloadNow@0
    DllGetClassObject@12
